cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact commit or archived version used. This is development research software, not a security-certified cryptosystem."
type: software
title: "CPWI: finite-instance experiments and structural audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Filardo
    given-names: Gautier-Edouard
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8310-2065"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gautierfilardo-efrei/cpwi-post-quantum-dynamical-inversion"
url: "https://github.com/gautierfilardo-efrei/cpwi-post-quantum-dynamical-inversion"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and finite-instance diagnostics for coupled
  permutation-word inversion. Includes independent reproduction checks,
  collision propagation, layered random-map comparisons, a bounded-state
  inversion algorithm, endpoint-distance checks and exploratory invariant
  statistics. These materials do not establish classical or post-quantum
  security and do not define a deployable cryptosystem.
keywords:
  - permutation groups
  - inversion
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - reproducibility
  - cryptanalysis
